  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry and seasonable conditions continue through \nearly next week, with frost possible this weekend.\n\nSurface high pressure remains to the north through Saturday with\ndry and seasonable conditions expected to continue. High \ntemperatures today will be in the 60s for most with only highest\nelevations staying in the 50s. Tonight, low temperatures will \nbe in the upper 30s to 40s. For Friday and Saturday, surface \nhigh pressure extends southward from Canada with dry cold fronts\nbringing in cooler air. High temperatures stay in the 50s to \nlow 60s while overnight lows plummet into the 30s for most. The \nexception will be east of the I-95 corridor where low \ntemperatures stay in the low 40s. Frost is possible Friday and \nSaturday night. \n\nHigh pressure will continue to build southward into the region \nSunday through Tuesday. Dry conditions and seasonable \ntemperatures expected each day with light north to east winds. A\nbackdoor cold front could try to push into the region Tuesday \ninto Tuesday night, but will have very little to no moisture \nwith it to produce any precipitation. A surge of cooler \ntemperatures will follow behind the front for the day on \nWednesday.",
